        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Songs: If My Friends Could See Me Now\n- Musicals: Sweet Charity, Times Square\n- People: Cy Coleman, Dorothy Fields, Neil Simon, Bob Fosse, Gwen Verdon, John McMartin\n- Characters: Charity, Vittorio\n\nFacts:\n- Cy Coleman wrote the music, Dorothy Fields wrote the lyrics, and Neil Simon wrote the book for the 1966 musical referred to here as Times Square.\n- Bob Fosse directed and choreographed Times Square.\n- Gwen Verdon starred in Times Square alongside John McMartin.\n- Gwen Verdon was Bob Fosse’s wife and muse.\n- “If My Friends Could See Me Now” is a song from the 1966 musical Times Square.\n- In “If My Friends Could See Me Now,” the character Charity reflects on her marvelous luck while spending time with Vittorio.",
