        "original_id": "06207459-19a6-51cf-89a7-51b8916eb1a7",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Songs: \"If My Friends Could See Me Now\"\n- Musicals and films: \"Sweet Charity\"\n- People: Cy Coleman, Dorothy Fields, Gwen Verdon, Shirley MacLaine, Bob Fosse, John McMartin, Vittorio\n\nFacts:\n- \"If My Friends Could See Me Now\" is a song from the 1966 Broadway musical \"Sweet Charity\".\n- Cy Coleman wrote the music for \"If My Friends Could See Me Now\", and Dorothy Fields wrote its lyrics.\n- In the original New York cast of \"Sweet Charity\", Gwen Verdon played Charity.\n- In \"Sweet Charity\", the character Charity reflects on her marvellous luck while spending time with Vittorio during \"If My Friends Could See Me Now\".\n- Bob Fosse directed and choreographed the Broadway production of \"Sweet Charity\".\n- Gwen Verdon and John McMartin starred in the Broadway production of \"Sweet Charity\".\n- In the 1969 film adaptation of \"Sweet Charity\", Shirley MacLaine performed \"If My Friends Could See Me Now\".",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
